    "title": "The idempotent charge path — first request vs replay",
    "legend": [
      {
        "tone": "accent",
        "label": "atomic: key reserve + effect in one transaction"
      },
      {
        "tone": "success",
        "label": "the keys store — enforces exactly-once"
      },
      {
        "tone": "warning",
        "label": "external effect that must run only once"
      },
      {
        "tone": "muted",
        "label": "the replay path — short-circuits to stored result"
      }
    ],
    "subtitle": "Client sends Idempotency-Key. The handler reserves the key and writes the charge in ONE transaction; the unique constraint on the keys store is what enforces exactly-once. A replay hits the stored result and skips the gateway entirely. The failure path is the dashed retry; the repair is the keys store."
  },
